libFuzzer support for QuickJS
=============================

Build the fuzzing targets with CMake. clang is required: it is the compiler that
ships the libFuzzer runtime.

  cmake -B build -DQUICKJS_FUZZER=ON -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang
  cmake --build build

This can be extended with sanitizer support to improve efficacy:

  cmake -B build -DQUICKJS_FUZZER=ON -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang \
    -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS="-fsanitize=address" -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS="-fsanitize=address"


Currently, there are seven fuzzing targets defined: fuzz_eval, fuzz_compile,
fuzz_bytecode, fuzz_json, fuzz_regexp, fuzz_regexp_compile and
fuzz_module_export. The above build command will produce an executable binary
for each of them in build/, which can be simply executed as:

  ./build/fuzz_eval

or with an initial corpus:

  ./build/fuzz_compile corpus_dir/

or with a predefined dictionary to improve its efficacy:

  ./build/fuzz_eval -dict fuzz/fuzz.dict

or with arbitrary CLI arguments provided by libFuzzer (https://llvm.org/docs/LibFuzzer.html).
